Overlay 0040 (rev2 — the "renders at native" claim was WRONG: the game
shipped SUB-NATIVE, fixed by 0041 SSAA; this line now points at the real
Supersampling control). reference 0024 ported to MM's BenMenu: Internal
Resolution display on iOS/visionOS. The slider's only consumer,
Window::SetResolutionMultiplier -> Fast3dGui's ImGui game-window viewport,
NEVER runs on iOS/visionOS — these builds always render at the display's
native drawable (iPhone A/B verified identical pixels at 100%/200%; Vision
Pro log-verified 3840x2160). A slider stuck at "100%" reads as half-res to
anyone who knows desktop 2S2H, and persisting a multiplier is a landmine:
it scales POINTS, so if a future LUS pin ever activates the consumer it
would SHRINK the render. Replace the dead slider with a static truth line
on __IOS__ (covers visionOS — same define, overlay 0027).
MM delta vs reference: BenMenu's widget is the "%.0f%%" format string with a
PreFunc/Callback chain (SohGui's was plainer); the whole AddWidget(...)
statement is wrapped, not just the slider tail.

--- a/mm/2s2h/BenGui/BenMenu.cpp
+++ b/mm/2s2h/BenGui/BenMenu.cpp
@@ -552,6 +552,7 @@
     AddWidget(path, "Toggle Fullscreen", WIDGET_BUTTON)
         .Callback([](WidgetInfo& info) { Ship::Context::GetRawInstance()->GetWindow()->ToggleFullscreen(); })
         .Options(ButtonOptions().Tooltip("Toggles Fullscreen On/Off."));
+#ifndef __IOS__
     AddWidget(path, "Internal Resolution: %.0f%%", WIDGET_CVAR_SLIDER_FLOAT)
         .CVar(CVAR_INTERNAL_RESOLUTION)
         .Callback([](WidgetInfo& info) {
@@ -576,6 +577,14 @@
                 .Format("")
                 .Min(0.5f)
                 .Max(2.0f));
+#else
+    // SOH_IOS (overlay 0040): the multiplier's only consumer is the desktop
+    // ImGui game-window viewport, which never runs on iOS/visionOS — these
+    // builds always render at the display's native drawable (device-verified;
+    // Vision Pro: 3840x2160). Show the truth instead of a dead slider.
+    AddWidget(path, "Internal Resolution: use Supersampling (SSAA) in the iOS settings — this desktop slider has no effect here",
+              WIDGET_SEPARATOR_TEXT);
+#endif
 #ifndef __WIIU__
